Even in a non-speed-game, magic missile is much more effective per
mana. In a speed run, Orcus' wand can be recharged after he brings you
the Amulet, which is perfectly sufficient for those cases where you
really do want a zap of death.


A few more notes: While it makes sense in a conventional game, speed
runners generally move fast enough so that you can afford to kill
Rodney before you find the vibrating square. You even save quite a few
turns that way.

If you have everything else prepared, you can save a few turns and
scrolls if you do the Invocation only after you lure Orcus to the
vibrating level. Sure, he will waste a few charges on those six turns
you foo-port and invoke, but you're magic resistant from the Eye
anyway.

Maud sometimes uses Asmodeus instead because he deals 78% more damage
per turn to the High Priest, but I like to pay off Asmodeus.

Covetous monsters won't follow you if they are fleeing. That is a long-
lasting condition caused by scaring them: Elbereth, Magicbane special
effects, instruments, taking damage, etc. So don't do that to Orcus.


